============================================================================================
READOUT
============================================================================================
The raw atom absolute sum is the old free-envelope shadow.  The block L2 and L1 columns retain the exact transfer channel s and the 6x6 residue matrix before absolute values.  When these ratios are much smaller than raw/signed, the missing proof should be a channelwise Cauchy/Schur estimate plus a successive-minima count over s, not a direct six-dimensional harmonic bound.
Conjectural simplification: prove a uniform bound on sum_s ||Core_s||_2 ||Pair_s(A,B)||_2 for the two-large tail after height-2 wall deletion.  HYP-2632 supplies the finite packet phase; this script supplies the exact transfer skeleton that the analytic bound should use.

